-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Databricks SQL and Python code must be updated to use three-level namespace (`catalog.schema.table`) when referencing tables, rather than the legacy `schema.table` pattern. If your code hardcodes hive_metastore or only expects two-level naming, refactoring is required. 
-- MAGIC

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### A1. Setting Default Catalog
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Setting a default catalog can potentially reduce the impact on required code changes, if the schema names within the catalog are reflective of how they were in the HMS.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Depending on the context, there are three mechanisms for doing this.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC #### Execution context
-- MAGIC In notebooks, add a `USE CATALOG` statement before making any two-level references; these references will be relative to the specified catalog.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC This setting is scoped to the execution context. If you disconnect and reconnect, you need to rerun `USE CATALOG`. 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC #### Cluster context
-- MAGIC If you own the cluster or have `CAN MANAGE`, you can set a default catalog at the cluster level, via a Spark configuration setting (this can also be factored into a compute policy for automation, if desired).
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #1976d2; background: #e3f2fd; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">ℹ️</span>
-- MAGIC     <div>
-- MAGIC       This approach only works for classic clusters. You cannot set this on serverless or SQL warehouses.
-- MAGIC     </div>
-- MAGIC   </div>
-- MAGIC </div>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC #### Workspace context
-- MAGIC Workspace admins can also set the default catalog at the workspace level, which would automatically apply to any workloads running in the context of the workspace.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ### A2. Views and UDFs
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC These same principles apply to views and functions. All views and functions must be recreated in UC after the referenced base tables are migrated. 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Consider also how to organize views and functions:
-- MAGIC - Organize views/functions with their referenced objects?
-- MAGIC - Collect views/functions in a dedicated schema?

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ## B. Storage Access
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Any path references (through DBFS mounts or direct cloud path references) will need to be revisited, as Unity Catalog does not support DBFS or the `ANY FILE` securable.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC The overall approach:
-- MAGIC - create storage credentials for each cloud storage location
-- MAGIC - map external locations in to subdivide the storage locations as needed
-- MAGIC - create volumes associated with those external locations where file access is needed
-- MAGIC - refactor code to use volume paths
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="display:flex; justify-content:center;">
